WEBVTT

00:01:57.916 --> 00:02:00.316
and "nine out of these 10 dentists agree."

00:02:00.356 --> 00:02:02.996
Size matters and so does methodology.

00:02:03.036 --> 00:02:05.156
According to the American
Dental Association,

00:02:05.196 --> 00:02:08.636
there are about 200,000
registered dentists in the US.

00:02:08.636 --> 00:02:10.836
I’m not going to bore you
with the maths here,

00:02:10.836 --> 00:02:13.956
but to get a statistically significant
sample of 200,000 people,

00:02:13.996 --> 00:02:15.316
you need about 400.

00:02:15.356 --> 00:02:18.916
So if you're reading in the fine print
that only 50 dentists were surveyed,

00:02:18.956 --> 00:02:21.116
you know that's not
statistically significant.

00:02:21.156 --> 00:02:22.556
It's just a marketing ploy.

00:02:22.556 --> 00:02:24.596
So the next time you see one of these ads,

00:02:24.596 --> 00:02:25.756
ask yourself:

00:02:25.796 --> 00:02:27.436
What were people actually asked?

00:02:27.476 --> 00:02:28.676
What's gone unsaid?

00:02:28.716 --> 00:02:30.596
And what was the survey context?